make_local_cache	void	size_t size, int64 entries, size_t key, size_t entry	raises	nocatalog	allocating raises only when memory runs out, and the table is made first and kept, so a failed allocation leaves no cache without its table; it reads no catalog	HASHCTL info = {.keysize = key, .entrysize = entry}; if (doltgres_local_cache_table == NULL) doltgres_local_cache_table = hash_create("versioned local node cache", entries, &info, HASH_ELEM | HASH_BLOBS); doltgres_local_cache = MemoryContextAllocExtended(TopMemoryContext, size, MCXT_ALLOC_HUGE | MCXT_ALLOC_ZERO)	test/t/009_cache.pl: a temporary node is cached in the backend's own cache
local_cache_base	void *		noraise	nocatalog	doltgres_local_cache is a variable	doltgres_local_cache	test/t/009_cache.pl: a temporary node is cached in the backend's own cache
