scan_restart	void	TableScanDesc scan, ScanKey key, bool set_params, bool allow_strat, bool allow_sync, bool allow_pagemode	raises	nocatalog	it does what heap_rescan does outside heap's pages: its flag updates under set_params, SO_ALLOW_PAGEMODE only with an MVCC snapshot, then initscan's copy of the keys into the scan's array, keeping the count begin set, and its pgstat_count_heap_scan for a seq scan, which allocates the relation's pending entry the first time it counts; it reads no catalog	if (set_params) { if (allow_strat) scan->rs_flags |= SO_ALLOW_STRAT; else scan->rs_flags &= ~SO_ALLOW_STRAT; if (allow_sync) scan->rs_flags |= SO_ALLOW_SYNC; else scan->rs_flags &= ~SO_ALLOW_SYNC; if (allow_pagemode && scan->rs_snapshot && IsMVCCSnapshot(scan->rs_snapshot)) scan->rs_flags |= SO_ALLOW_PAGEMODE; else scan->rs_flags &= ~SO_ALLOW_PAGEMODE; } if (key != NULL && scan->rs_nkeys > 0) memcpy(scan->rs_key, key, scan->rs_nkeys * sizeof(ScanKeyData)); if (scan->rs_flags & SO_TYPE_SEQSCAN) pgstat_count_heap_scan(scan->rs_rd); memset(&((DoltgresScan *) scan)->worker, 0, sizeof(ParallelBlockTableScanWorkerData))	test/t/033_scan.pl: a seq scan of a table on the fork's storage gives its base's rows
