btree_compare	int	DgCompared compared, DgBytes a, DgBytes b	raises	catalog	it runs a btree class's comparison function, user code that can raise and read any catalog, in a memory context of its own, a child of the caller's made for the call and deleted after it, so nothing the function allocates outlives the call and a comparison nested inside it has its own; a by-value argument is its word's bytes, low byte first, and any other its stored bytes, a varlena's without its header, copied into that context, aligned	MemoryContext cxt = AllocSetContextCreate(CurrentMemoryContext, "doltgres comparison", ALLOCSET_SMALL_SIZES); MemoryContext old = MemoryContextSwitchTo(cxt); FmgrInfo f; Datum x[2]; DgBytes v[2] = {a, b}; fmgr_info_cxt(compared.function, &f, cxt); for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) { if (compared.byval) { Datum w = 0; for (size_t j = 0; j < v[i].len && j < sizeof(Datum); j++) w |= (Datum) (unsigned char) v[i].data[j] << (8 * j); x[i] = w; } else if (compared.typlen == -1) { struct varlena *p = palloc(VARHDRSZ + v[i].len); SET_VARSIZE(p, VARHDRSZ + v[i].len); memcpy(VARDATA(p), v[i].data, v[i].len); x[i] = PointerGetDatum(p); } else { char *p = palloc(v[i].len); memcpy(p, v[i].data, v[i].len); x[i] = PointerGetDatum(p); } } *out = DatumGetInt32(FunctionCall2Coll(&f, compared.collation, x[0], x[1])); MemoryContextSwitchTo(old); MemoryContextDelete(cxt)	test/t/034_compared.pl: many comparisons through a row-type key leave the entry's context flat
