key_settle_open	void	Oid table	raises	catalog	get_rel_relkind reads the relation's pg_class row, passing over one that no longer exists and any relation but a table, try_table_open takes no lock, since the statement that altered the table or changed its key holds it, and reads its relcache entry, and the settle under it reads the catalog	{ char kind = get_rel_relkind(table); if (RELKIND_HAS_TABLE_AM(kind)) { Relation rel = try_table_open(table, NoLock); if (rel != NULL) { doltgres_key_settle_table(rel); table_close(rel, NoLock); } } }	test/t/047_rewrite.pl: ADD PRIMARY KEY writes a table with rows once under its new key
key_new_file	void	Relation rel	raises	catalog	RelationSetNewRelfilenumber gives the table and its TOAST relation new relfilenodes through their routine and updates their pg_class rows, and table_open locks the TOAST relation as the table is locked	{ RelationSetNewRelfilenumber(rel, rel->rd_rel->relpersistence); if (OidIsValid(rel->rd_rel->reltoastrelid)) { Relation toast = table_open(rel->rd_rel->reltoastrelid, AccessExclusiveLock); RelationSetNewRelfilenumber(toast, toast->rd_rel->relpersistence); table_close(toast, NoLock); } }	test/t/047_rewrite.pl: ADD PRIMARY KEY writes a table with rows once under its new key
